  "id": "Wandsworth-2026_0068",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Installation of 1No. BT Street Hub Unit and associated advertisement panels on either side of the unit",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - By reason of lack of information provided and the presence of similar 'Street Hubs' in the immediate area, the proposal is considered to constitute unnecessary street clutter that would cause harm to visual amenity and local spatial character, contrary to London Plan D8 and Local Plan Policies LP1 and LP9.",
    "Reason : 2 - By reason of its design, scale and siting, it is considered that the proposal would represent a safety hazard and would create an increased obstruction on the footway which may further impair access to the cycle stands and the nearby bus stop for groups with mobility impairments. It is therefore considered that the proposal would cause material harm to public safety, contrary to London Plan Policy T4, LP9 and LP50.",
    "Reason : 3 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to work with the applicant in a positive and proactive manner and the Council has, as far as practicable, sought solutions to problems arising in relation to dealing with the planning application. We have made available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan consisting of the Core Strategy, Development Management Policies Document, Supplementary Planning documents and where appropriate the Site Specific Allocations Document as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the principle of the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal.\r\n"
  ],
